@startuml sequence_diagram_allergen_localization
title WEB02 - SD 5: Display localized allergen names by stable ID
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "System User" as User
participant FeatureView as Page
participant apiClient as Client
participant BackEndAPI as API
participant AllergenNameSource as Source
participant AllergenLabel as Label
participant LocaleProvider as Locale
participant FeedbackView as Feedback

note over Page,Source
    WEB05 page is already authorized under WEB03.
    The WEB05 adapter uses approved back-end labels by stable ID.
    The allergen API response below is proposed in Q4.
    WEB05 and the API owners must confirm it before implementation.
end note
User -> Page : Open product detail
Page -> Client : get(/catalogue/:productId, options)
Client -> API : GET /api/v1/catalogue/:productId
alt Business data request succeeds
    API --> Client : Product and category text, allergens with ID and name
    Client --> Page : Product DTO
    Page -> Source : loadFor(allergenIds)
    opt Allergen labels not already loaded for this view
        Source -> Client : get(/allergens)
        Client -> API : GET /api/v1/allergens
        API --> Client : Allergen records with ID, name and proposed labels, or error
        Client --> Source : Allergen list or ApiError
    end
    Source --> Page : Available PT/EN labels by stable ID, or source unavailable
    Page -> Page : Build display data, preserve product and category text
    loop Each allergen on first render and on locale change
        Page -> Label : render(allergen)
        Label -> Locale : Read active locale
        Locale --> Label : pt-PT or en-GB
        alt Label for selected locale is available
            Label --> User : Display localized name for the same allergen ID
        else Label missing or source unavailable
            Label -> Feedback : render(translationUnavailable, sourceName)
            Feedback --> User : Identify the stored name and explain that translation is unavailable
        end
    end
else Business data request fails
    API --> Client : Error response
    Client --> Page : ApiError
    Page -> Feedback : Render safe localized failure and recovery action
    Feedback --> User : Report catalogue loading failure
end
note over Page,Locale
    Changing locale selects a label from the current read model.
    A missing label remains an AC 3 acceptance gap for that data.
end note
@enduml
